            question:
              'Consider the function $$f$$ defined by $$f(x) = \\ln(x^2-16)$$ for $$x>4$$. The graph of $$f$$ crosses the x-axis at point A$$(a,0)$$. The line $$L$$ is the tangent to the graph of $$f$$ at the point B.\n (a) Find the exact value of $$a$$. [3]\n (b) Given that the gradient of $$L$$ is $$\\dfrac{1}{3}$$, find the x-coordinate of B. [6]',
            answer: '(a) $$a = \\sqrt{17}$$\n (b) $$x = 8$$',
