            question:
              'Consider the graph of the function $$f(x) = x + \\dfrac{12}{x^2}$$, $$x\\neq0$$.\n (a)(i) Write down the zero of $$f(x)$$. [2]\n (a)(ii) Write down the coordinates of the local minimum point. [2]\n (b) Consider the function $$g(x)=3-x$$. Solve $$f(x)=g(x)$$. [2]',
            answer: '(a)(i) $$x\\approx-2.29$$ (a)(ii) $$(2.88, 4.33)$$ (b) $$x\\approx-1.43$$',
