            calculator: false,
            question:
              'Consider the vectors $$\\mathbf{a}=\\begin{pmatrix}3\\\\2p\\end{pmatrix}$$ and $$\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{pmatrix}p+1\\\\8\\end{pmatrix}$$.\n Find the possible values of $$p$$ for which $$\\mathbf{a}$$ and $$\\mathbf{b}$$ are parallel.',
            answer: '$$p=-4$$ or $$p=3$$',
            solution:
              'Parallel vectors are scalar multiples: $$3(8)=2p(p+1) \\Rightarrow 2p^2+2p-24=0 \\Rightarrow p^2+p-12=0 \\Rightarrow (p+4)(p-3)=0$$.\n So $$p=-4$$ or $$p=3$$.',
            questionType: 'Vectors',
            diagram: null,
            subtopicSlug: 'mixed-topics',
