            question:
              'The function $$f$$ is defined by $$f(x) = \\dfrac{2x+4}{3-x}$$, where $$x\\in\\mathbb{R},\\ x\\neq3$$.\n (a)(i) Write down the equation of the vertical asymptote of the graph of $$f$$. [1]\n (a)(ii) Write down the equation of the horizontal asymptote of the graph of $$f$$. [1]\n (b)(i) Find the coordinates where the graph of $$f$$ crosses the x-axis. [1]\n (b)(ii) Find the coordinates where the graph of $$f$$ crosses the y-axis. [1]\n (c) Sketch the graph of $$f$$ on a set of axes. [1]',
