              'The function $$f$$ is of the form $$f(x) = ax+b+\\dfrac{c}{x}$$, where $$a$$, $$b$$ and $$c$$ are positive integers. Part of the graph of $$y=f(x)$$ is shown; it has a local maximum at $$(-2,-2)$$ and a local minimum at $$(2,6)$$.\n (a) On the axes, draw the line $$y=-6$$. [1]\n (b) Write down the number of solutions to $$f(x)=-6$$. [1]\n (c) Find the range of values of $$k$$ for which $$f(x)=k$$ has no solution. [2]',
