            question:
              "Olivia's house consists of four vertical walls and a sloping roof made from two rectangles. The height, CD, from the ground to the base of the roof is 4.5 m. The base angles of the roof are $$A\\hat{B}C=27^\\circ$$ and $$A\\hat{C}B=26^\\circ$$. The house is 10 m long and 5 m wide. The length AC is approximately 2.84 m. Olivia decides to put solar panels on the roof, fitted to both sides. Each panel is 1.6 m long and 0.95 m wide, arranged in uniform rows with the shorter edge parallel to AB or AC; each panel must be at least 0.3 m from the edge of the roof and the top of the roof, AF. Olivia estimates the solar panels will cover an area of $$29\\text{ m}^2$$.\n (a) Find the length AB, giving your answer to four significant figures.\n (b) Find the total area of the two rectangles that make up the roof.\n (c) Find the maximum number of complete panels that can be fitted to the whole roof.\n (d) Find the percentage error in her estimate.\n (e) Olivia investigates arranging the panels such that the longer edge of each panel is parallel to AB or AC. State whether this new arrangement will allow Olivia to fit more solar panels to the roof. Justify your answer.",
