            question:
              'A factory packages coconut water in cone-shaped containers with a base radius of $$5.2$$ cm and a height of $$13$$ cm. The factory designers are investigating whether a cone-shaped container can be replaced with a cylinder-shaped container with the same radius and the same total surface area.\n (a) Find the volume of one cone-shaped container.\n (b) Find the slant height of the cone-shaped container.\n (c) Show that the total surface area of the cone-shaped container is $$314\\text{ cm}^2$$, correct to three significant figures.\n (d) Find the height, $$h$$, of this cylinder-shaped container.\n (e) The factory director wants to increase the volume of coconut water sold per container. State whether or not they should replace the cone-shaped containers with cylinder-shaped containers. Justify your conclusion.',
            answer:
              '(a) $$V=368\\text{ cm}^3$$ (b) slant height $$=14.0$$ cm (d) $$h=4.41$$ cm (e) Yes, replace — cylinder volume ($$375\\text{ cm}^3$$) exceeds cone volume ($$368\\text{ cm}^3$$)',
