            question:
              'Two straight fences meet at point A and a field lies between them. A horse is tied to a post, P, by a rope of length $$r$$ metres. Point D is on one fence and point E is on the other, such that $$PD=PE=PA=r$$ and $$D\\hat{P}E=\\theta$$ radians. The length of the arc DE shown in the diagram is 28 m. A new fence is to be constructed between points B and C which will enclose the field. Point C is due west of B and $$AC=800$$ m. The bearing of B from A is $$195^\\circ$$.\n (a) Write down an expression for $$r$$ in terms of $$\\theta$$.\n (b) Show that the area of the field that the horse can reach is $$\\dfrac{392}{\\theta^2}(\\theta+\\sin\\theta)$$.\n (c) The area of field that the horse can reach is $$460\\text{ m}^2$$. Find the value of $$\\theta$$.\n (d) Hence, find the size of $$D\\hat{A}E$$.\n (e)(i) Find the size of $$A\\hat{B}C$$.\n (e)(ii) Find the length of new fence required.',
