            question:
              'A company produces bags of sugar with mass normally distributed, mean 1000 g, standard deviation 3.5 g. A bag is rejected if its mass is less than 995 g.\n a. Find the probability that a bag selected at random is rejected. [2]\n b. Estimate the number of bags rejected from a random sample of 100 bags. [1]\n c. Given that a bag is not rejected, find the probability that it has a mass greater than 1005 g. [3]',
