            question:
              'SpeedWay airline flies from city A to city B; flight time is normally distributed, mean 260 minutes, standard deviation 15 minutes. A flight is late if it takes longer than 275 minutes and on time if between $$m$$ and 275 minutes, with $$P(\\text{on time})=0.830$$. During a week, SpeedWay has 12 flights from A to B, independent of each other.\n a. Calculate the probability a flight is not late. [2]\n b. Find the value of $$m$$. [3]\n c.(i) Calculate the probability that at least 7 of the 12 flights are on time. [3]\n c.(ii) Given at least 7 flights are on time, find the probability that exactly 10 are on time. [4]\n d. SpeedWay increases flights to 20 per week and improves efficiency; the probability at least 19 flights are on time is 0.788. A flight is chosen at random; calculate the probability it is on time. [3]',
            answer:
              'a. $$0.841$$ b. $$m\\approx226$$ min c.(i) $$0.991$$ (ii) $$0.299$$ d. $$p\\approx0.957$$',
            solution:
              'a. $$P(X<275)=1-0.158655=0.841344\\approx0.841$$.\n b. $$P(X<275)-P(X<m)=0.830 \\Rightarrow P(X<m)=0.0113447 \\Rightarrow m=225.820\\approx226$$ min.\n c. $$X\\sim B(12,0.83)$$: $$P(X\\ge7)=0.991248\\approx0.991$$; $$P(X=10\\mid X\\ge7)=\\dfrac{P(X=10)}{P(X\\ge7)}=\\dfrac{0.295952}{0.991248}=0.299$$.\n d. Solve $$\\binom{20}{19}p^{19}(1-p)+p^{20}=0.788$$ numerically/graphically: $$p\\approx0.957$$.',
