            solution:
              'a. $$P(T>40)=0.25 \\Rightarrow z=0.674489 \\Rightarrow \\sigma=\\dfrac{5}{0.674489}=7.413\\approx7.41$$ min.\n b. $$P(T>45)=0.0886718\\approx0.0887$$.\n c. $$L\\sim B(5,0.0886718)$$: $$P(L\\ge1)=1-P(L=0)=0.371$$.\n d. $$P(L<3\\mid L\\ge1)=\\dfrac{P(L=1)+P(L=2)}{P(L\\ge1)}=\\dfrac{0.36532}{0.37140}=0.984$$.\n e. Needs to be on time at least 5 of the remaining 6 days ($$20-15=5$$ more, out of 6 remaining): $$X\\sim B(6,0.911328)$$: $$P(X\\ge5)=0.907$$.',
            questionType: 'Normal distribution, Binomial distribution, conditional probability',
            diagram: null,
            subtopicSlug: 'normal-distribution',
