              "Let $$f(x) = \\frac{1}{3}x^3 + x^2 - 15x + 17$$. The graph of $$f$$ has horizontal tangents at the points where $$x=a$$ and $$x=b$$, $$a<b$$.\n (a) Find $$f'(x)$$. [2]\n (b) Find the value of $$a$$ and the value of $$b$$. [3]\n (c)(i) Sketch the graph of $$y=f'(x)$$. [1]\n (c)(ii) Hence explain why the graph of $$f$$ has a local maximum point at $$x=a$$. [1]\n (d)(i) Find $$f''(x)$$. [3]\n (d)(ii) Hence, use your answer to part (d)(i) to show that the graph of $$f$$ has a local minimum point at $$x=b$$. [1]\n (e) The normal to the graph of $$f$$ at $$x=a$$ and the tangent to the graph of $$f$$ at $$x=b$$ intersect at the point $$(p,q)$$. Find the value of $$p$$ and the value of $$q$$. [5]",
