            question:
              "The following diagram shows a ball attached to the end of a spring, suspended from a ceiling. The height, $$h$$ metres, of the ball above the ground at time $$t$$ seconds after being released can be modelled by $$h(t)=0.4\\cos(\\pi t)+1.8$$ where $$t\\ge0$$.\n (a) Find the height of the ball above the ground when it is released. [2]\n (b) Find the minimum height of the ball above the ground. [2]\n (c) Show that the ball takes 2 seconds to return to its initial height above the ground for the first time. [2]\n (d) For the first 2 seconds of its motion, determine the amount of time that the ball is less than $$1.8+0.2\\sqrt{2}$$ metres above the ground. [5]\n (e) Find the rate of change of the ball's height above the ground when $$t=\\frac13$$. Give your answer in the form $$p\\pi\\sqrt{q}\\ \\text{ms}^{-1}$$ where $$p\\in\\mathbb{Q}$$ and $$q\\in\\mathbb{Z}^+$$. [4]",
