            question:
              'Consider the function $$f$$ defined by $$f(x)=6+6\\cos x$$, for $$0\\le x\\le4\\pi$$. The graph of $$f$$ touches the $$x$$-axis at points A and B. The shaded region is enclosed by the graph of $$y=f(x)$$ and the $$x$$-axis, between A and B. The right cone in the following diagram has a total surface area of $$12\\pi$$, equal to the shaded area. The cone has base radius 2, height $$h$$, and slant height $$l$$.\n (a) Find the $$x$$-coordinates of A and B. [3]\n (b) Show that the area of the shaded region is $$12\\pi$$. [5]\n (c) Find the value of $$l$$. [3]\n (d) Hence, find the volume of the cone. [4]',
