            calculator: true,
            question:
              'Particle A travels in a straight line such that its displacement, $$s$$ metres, from a fixed origin after $$t$$ seconds is given by $$s(t)=8t-t^2$$, for $$0\\le t\\le10$$. Particle A starts at the origin and passes through the origin again when $$t=p$$. Particle A changes direction when $$t=q$$. The total distance travelled by particle A is given by $$d$$.\n (a) Find the value of $$p$$. [2]\n (b)(i) Find the value of $$q$$. [2]\n (b)(ii) Find the displacement of particle A from the origin when $$t=q$$. [2]\n (c) Find the distance of particle A from the origin when $$t=10$$. [2]\n (d) Find the value of $$d$$. [2]\n (e) A second particle, particle B, travels along the same straight line such that its velocity is given by $$v(t)=14-2t$$, for $$t\\ge0$$. When $$t=k$$, the distance travelled by particle B is equal to $$d$$. Find the value of $$k$$. [4]',
