            question:
              'A small cuboid box has a rectangular base of length $$3x$$ cm and width $$x$$ cm, where $$x>0$$. The height is $$y$$ cm, where $$y>0$$. The sum of the length, width and height is 12 cm. The volume of the box is $$V\\,\\text{cm}^3$$.\n (a) Write down an expression for $$y$$ in terms of $$x$$. [1]\n (b) Find an expression for $$V$$ in terms of $$x$$. [2]\n (c) Find $$\\dfrac{dV}{dx}$$. [2]\n (d)(i) Find the value of $$x$$ for which $$V$$ is a maximum. [4]\n (d)(ii) Justify your answer. [3]\n (e) Find the maximum volume. [2]',
