            question:
              'The following table shows the probability distribution of a discrete random variable $$A$$, in terms of an angle $$\\theta$$.\n $$P(A=1)=\\cos\\theta,\\quad P(A=2)=2\\cos2\\theta$$\n (a) Show that $$\\cos\\theta=\\dfrac34$$. [6]\n (b) Given that $$\\tan\\theta>0$$, find $$\\tan\\theta$$. [3]\n (c) Let $$y=\\dfrac{1}{\\cos x}$$, for $$0<x<\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}$$. The graph of $$y$$ between $$x=\\theta$$ and $$x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}$$ is rotated $$360°$$ about the $$x$$-axis. Find the volume of the solid formed. [6]',
            answer:
              '(b) $$\\tan\\theta=\\dfrac{\\sqrt7}{3}$$\n (c) Volume $$=\\pi\\left(1-\\dfrac{\\tan\\theta}{4}\\right)$$ evaluated $$=\\pi\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi-\\theta}{3}\\sqrt7\\right)$$ (see working)',
