            calculator: true,
            question:
              'Let $$f(x)=\\ln x$$ and $$g(x)=3+\\ln\\left(\\dfrac{x}{2}\\right)$$, for $$x>0$$. The graph of $$g$$ can be obtained from the graph of $$f$$ by a horizontal stretch of scale factor $$q$$ followed by a translation of $$\\begin{pmatrix}h\\\\k\\end{pmatrix}$$.\n Let $$h(x)=g(x)\\times\\cos(0.1x)$$, for $$0<x<4$$. The graph of $$h$$ and the line $$y=x$$ are shown; $$h$$ intersects $$h^{-1}$$ at $$x=0.111$$ and $$x=3.31$$ (3 s.f.).\n (a)(i) Write down the value of $$q$$. [1]\n (a)(ii) Write down the value of $$h$$. [1]\n (a)(iii) Write down the value of $$k$$. [1]\n (b)(i) Find $$\\displaystyle\\int_{0.111}^{3.31}\\big(h(x)-x\\big)dx$$. [2]\n (b)(ii) Hence, find the area of the region enclosed by the graphs of $$h$$ and $$h^{-1}$$. [3]\n (c) Let $$d$$ be the vertical distance from a point on the graph of $$h$$ to the line $$y=x$$. There is a point $$P(a,b)$$ on the graph of $$h$$ where $$d$$ is a maximum. Find the coordinates of $$P$$, where $$0.111<a<3.31$$. [7]',
            answer:
              '(a)(i) $$q=2$$ (a)(ii) $$h=0$$ (a)(iii) $$k=3$$\n (b)(i) $$2.40$$\n (b)(ii) $$5.45$$\n (c) $$P(0.974,2.27)$$',
            solution:
              "(a) Comparing $$g$$ to $$f$$: horizontal stretch factor $$q=2$$, translation $$(0,3)$$ (A1A1A1)\n (b)(i) GDC integration $$=2.40$$ (A2)\n (b)(ii) Using symmetry of $$h$$, $$h^{-1}$$ about $$y=x$$: area $$=2\\times2.40 =5.45$$ (M1M1A1)\n (c) $$d=h(x)-x$$; solve $$d'=0 \\Rightarrow x=0.974$$ (M1A1M1A2); substitute to get $$y=2.27$$ (M1A1)",
            questionType: 'Transformations / Inverse functions / Integration',
