            question:
              'A particle P moves along a straight line. Its velocity $$v_P$$ m s$$^{-1}$$ after $$t$$ seconds is $$v_P=\\sqrt{t}\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}t\\right)$$, for $$0\\le t\\le8$$.\n (a)(i) Write down the first value of $$t$$ at which P changes direction. [1]\n (a)(ii) Find the total distance travelled by P, for $$0\\le t\\le8$$. [2]\n (b) A second particle Q also moves along a straight line, with velocity $$v_Q=\\sqrt{t}$$ for $$0\\le t\\le8$$. After $$k$$ seconds, Q has travelled the same total distance as P. Find $$k$$. [4]',
