            question:
              'All lengths in this question are in metres. Let $$f(x)=-0.8x^2+0.5$$, for $$-0.5\\le x\\le0.5$$. Mark uses $$f(x)$$ as a model for a barrel. The region enclosed by the graph of $$f$$, the $$x$$-axis and the lines $$x=-0.5$$ and $$x=0.5$$ is rotated $$360°$$ about the $$x$$-axis.\n (a) Use the model to find the volume of the barrel. [3]\n (b) The empty barrel is filled with water. The volume $$V$$ m$$^3$$ of water in the barrel after $$t$$ minutes is $$V=0.8(1-e^{-0.1t})$$. How long will it take for the barrel to be half-full? [3]',
