            marksBreakdown: null,
            calculator: true,
            question:
              "A manufacturer makes trash cans in the form of a cylinder with a hemispherical top. The original trash can has height 70 cm and base radius 20 cm. A designer creates a new trash can, also cylinder + hemisphere, with height $$H$$ cm and base radius $$r$$ cm, subject to the constraint $$H+r=110$$ cm, maximising volume.\n (a) Write down the height of the cylinder (original can). [1]\n (b) Find the total volume of the original trash can. [4]\n (c) Find the height of the cylinder, $$h$$, of the new trash can, in terms of $$r$$. [2]\n (d) Show that the volume, $$V$$ cm$$^3$$, of the new trash can is given by $$V=110\\pi r^2-\\dfrac{7}{3}\\pi r^3$$. [3]\n (e) Using your GDC, find the value of $$r$$ which maximizes $$V$$. [2]\n (f) The designer claims the new trash can has a capacity at least 40% greater than the original. State whether the designer's claim is correct. Justify your answer. [4]",
            answer:
              '(a) $$50$$ cm\n (b) $$\\approx79600$$ cm$$^3$$\n (c) $$h=110-3r$$\n (e) $$r\\approx31.4$$ cm\n (f) Claim is correct (43.0% increase)',
            solution:
              '(a) Cylinder height $$=70-20=50$$ (A1)\n (b) $$V=\\pi(20)^2(50)+\\tfrac12\\cdot\\tfrac43\\pi(20)^3\\approx79600$$ (M1M1M1A1)\n (c) $$H+r=110 \\Rightarrow h=110-3r$$ (since $$H=h+r$$) (M1A1)\n (d) $$V=\\tfrac23\\pi r^3+\\pi r^2(110-3r)=110\\pi r^2-\\tfrac73\\pi r^3$$ (M1M1M1AG)\n (e) $$\\dfrac{dV}{dr}=0 \\Rightarrow r\\approx31.4$$ (M1A1)\n (f) $$V(31.4)\\approx114000$$; percentage increase $$\\approx43.0\\%>40\\%$$, so claim correct (M1A1R1A1)',
            questionType: 'Optimisation / Volume',
