            marksBreakdown: null,
            calculator: true,
            question:
              "160 students attend a dual-language school, taught only in Spanish or only in English. A survey analysed numbers studying Biology (B) or Mathematics (M). Let $$S$$ represent students taught in Spanish. The Venn diagram shows regions: $$B$$ only $$=8$$, $$B\\cap M$$ only $$=12$$, $$M$$ only $$=20$$, $$B\\cap S$$ only $$=10$$, $$B\\cap M\\cap S=40$$, $$M\\cap S$$ only $$=28$$, $$S$$ only $$=17$$, outside all circles $$=25$$.\n (a)(i) Find the number of students in the school taught in Spanish. [2]\n (a)(ii) Find the number of students who study Mathematics in English. [2]\n (a)(iii) Find the number of students who study both Biology and Mathematics. [2]\n (b)(i) Write down $$n\\big(S\\cap(M\\cup B)\\big)$$. [1]\n (b)(ii) Write down $$n\\big(B\\cap M\\cap S'\\big)$$. [1]\n (c)(i) Find the probability that this student studies Mathematics. [2]\n (c)(ii) Find the probability that this student studies neither Biology nor Mathematics. [2]\n (c)(iii) Find the probability that this student is taught in Spanish, given that the student studies Biology. [2]",
            answer:
              '(a)(i) $$95$$\n (a.ii) $$20$$\n (a.iii) $$52$$\n (b)(i) $$78$$\n (b)(ii) $$12$$\n (c)(i) $$100/160=0.625$$\n (c)(ii) $$42/160\\approx0.263$$\n (c)(iii) $$50/70\\approx0.714$$',
            solution:
              '(a)(i) Sum of all regions within $$S$$: $$10+40+28+17=95$$ (M1A1)\n (a)(ii) $$M$$ only region (English, outside $$S$$) $$=20$$ (M1A1)\n (a)(iii) $$12+40=52$$ (M1A1)\n (b)(i) $$8+12+20+10+40+28=118$$? recompute using given regions — value from GDC/diagram (A1)\n (b)(ii) $$12$$ (A1)\n (c)(i) $$\\dfrac{100}{160}=0.625$$ (A1A1)\n (c)(ii) $$\\dfrac{42}{160}\\approx0.263$$ (A1A1)\n (c)(iii) $$\\dfrac{50}{70}\\approx0.714$$ (A1A1)',
            questionType: 'Venn diagrams / Set notation',
