            calculator: true,
            question:
              'Contestants in a TV gameshow pass through three walls of doors (choosing at random), trying to avoid traps. First wall: 4 doors, 1 trap. Second wall: 5 doors, 2 traps. Third wall: 6 doors, 3 traps. Ayako and Natsuko are contestants (Natsuko second); contestants cannot watch each other play.\n (a) Write down the probability that Ayako avoids the trap in the first wall. [1]\n (b) Find the probability that only one of Ayako and Natsuko falls into a trap while attempting to pass through a door in the first wall. [3]\n (c) Copy the probability tree diagram and write down the relevant probabilities along the branches. [3]\n (d)(i) A contestant is chosen at random. Find the probability that this contestant fell into a trap while attempting to pass through a door in the second wall. [2]\n (d)(ii) A contestant is chosen at random. Find the probability that this contestant fell into a trap (overall). [3]\n (e) 120 contestants attempted this game. Find the expected number of contestants who fell into a trap while attempting to pass through a door in the third wall. [3]',
            answer:
              '(a) $$3/4$$\n (b) $$3/8=0.375$$\n (d)(i) $$3/10=0.3$$\n (d)(ii) $$93/120\\approx0.775$$\n (e) $$\\approx67.5$$',
            solution:
              '(a) $$1-\\dfrac14=\\dfrac34$$ (A1)\n (b) $$\\dfrac34\\times\\dfrac14+\\dfrac14\\times\\dfrac34=\\dfrac38$$ (M1M1A1)\n (c) Tree with probabilities $$\\tfrac14,\\tfrac34$$ then $$\\tfrac25,\\tfrac35$$ then $$\\tfrac36,\\tfrac36$$ (A1A1A1)\n (d)(i) $$\\dfrac34\\times\\dfrac25=0.3$$ (M1A1)\n (d)(ii) $$1-\\dfrac34\\times\\dfrac35\\times\\dfrac36=0.775$$ (M1M1A1)\n (e) $$\\dfrac34\\times\\dfrac35\\times\\dfrac36\\times120\\approx67.5$$ (M1M1A1)',
            questionType: 'Tree diagrams / Expected value',
