            question:
              'A random variable $$X$$ has probability density function\n $$f(x)=\\begin{cases}3a, & 0\\le x<2\\\\ a(x-5)(1-x), & 2\\le x\\le b\\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{cases}$$ where $$a,b\\in\\mathbb{R}^+,\\ 3<b\\le5$$.\n Consider the case where $$b=5$$.\n (a) Find, in terms of $$a$$, the probability that $$X$$ lies between 1 and 3. [4]\n (b) Sketch the graph of $$f$$. State the coordinates of the end points and any local maximum or minimum points, giving your answers in terms of $$a$$. [4]\n (c)(i) Find $$a$$. [4]\n (c)(ii) Find $$E(X)$$. [3]\n (c)(iii) Find the median of $$X$$. [4]',
