              'Two boats A and B travel due north. Initially, boat B is positioned 50 metres due east of boat A. The distances travelled by boat A and boat B, after $$t$$ seconds, are $$x$$ metres and $$y$$ metres respectively. The angle $$\\theta$$ is the radian measure of the bearing of boat B from boat A.\n a. Show that $$y=x+50\\cot\\theta$$. [1]\n b. At time $$T$$: Boat B has travelled 10 metres further than boat A. Boat B is travelling at double the speed of boat A. The rate of change of $$\\theta$$ is $$-0.1$$ radians per second. Find the speed of boat A at time $$T$$. [6]',
