            solution:
              'a. A quadratic function does not repeat periodically (daylight hours follow an annual cycle), or would predict negative/unbounded daylight over multiple years.\n b.i. Amplitude $$=\\dfrac{16-8}{2}=4$$.\n b.ii. Period $$=12$$ months.\n b.iii. Principal axis: $$y=12$$.\n c. Using amplitude, period ($$b=\\frac{360}{12}=30°$$) and reflection: $$f(t)=-4\\cos(30t)+12$$.\n d. Solve $$10.5=-4\\cos(30t)+12$$: two solutions in a 12-month period, giving duration $$\\approx7.47$$ months (7.46828…).\n e. Percentage error $$=\\left|\\dfrac{16-16\\frac{14}{60}}{16\\frac{14}{60}}\\right|\\times100=1.44\\%$$.',
