            subtopicDetail: 'Voronoi diagrams, coordinate geometry, cosine rule',
            difficulty: 'Hard',
            marks: 18,
            marksBreakdown: null,
            calculator: true,
            question:
              'The Voronoi diagram shows four supermarkets at $$A(0,0), B(6,0), C(0,6), D(2,2)$$; vertices X, Y, Z also shown (distances in km). The equation of $$(XY)$$ is $$y=2-x$$ and of $$(YZ)$$ is $$y=0.5x+3.5$$. The coordinates of Y are $$(-1,3)$$ and of Z are $$(7,7)$$. A town planner believes the larger the area of Voronoi cell XYZ, the more people will shop at supermarket D.\n a. Find the midpoint of $$[BD]$$.\n b. Find the equation of $$(XZ)$$.\n c. Find the coordinates of X.\n d. Determine the exact length of $$[YZ]$$.\n e. Given that the exact length of $$[XY]$$ is $$\\sqrt{32}$$, find the size of $$X\\hat{Y}Z$$ in degrees.\n f. Hence find the area of triangle XYZ.\n g. State one criticism of this interpretation.',
            answer:
              '$$(4,1);\\quad y=2x-7;\\quad X(3,-1);\\quad YZ=4\\sqrt5;\\quad X\\hat{Y}Z=71.6°;\\quad \\text{area}=24\\text{ km}^2$$',
            solution:
              "a. Midpoint of $$B(6,0)$$ and $$D(2,2)$$: $$\\left(\\dfrac{6+2}{2},\\dfrac{0+2}{2}\\right)=(4,1)$$.\n b. Perpendicular bisector of $$[BD]$$ passes through midpoint $$(4,1)$$ with gradient $$2$$ (negative reciprocal of $$BD$$'s gradient $$-\\frac12$$): $$y-1=2(x-4)\\Rightarrow y=2x-7$$.\n c. Solve $$y=2-x$$ and $$y=2x-7$$ simultaneously: $$X(3,-1)$$.\n d. Distance formula: $$YZ=\\sqrt{(7-(-1))^2+(7-3)^2}=\\sqrt{80}=4\\sqrt5$$.\n e. Cosine rule using $$XY=\\sqrt{32}$$, $$YZ=\\sqrt{80}$$, $$XZ=\\sqrt{80}$$: $$X\\hat YZ=71.6°$$ (71.5650…°).\n f. Area $$=\\frac12(\\sqrt{80})(\\sqrt{32})\\sin(71.565°)=24\\ \\text{km}^2$$.\n g. E.g. shopping choices may depend on factors other than proximity (price, specialization, transport links), so a larger Voronoi cell area does not guarantee more customers.",
