            question:
              'Points $$A(3,1)$$, $$B(3,5)$$, $$C(11,7)$$, $$D(9,1)$$ and $$E(7,3)$$ represent snow shelters in the Blackburn National Forest (horizontal and vertical scale: 1 unit = 1 km). The Park Ranger draws three straight lines to form an incomplete Voronoi diagram.\n (a) Calculate the gradient of the line segment $$AE$$. [2]\n (b) Find the equation of the line which would complete the Voronoi cell containing site $$E$$. Give your answer in the form $$ax+by+d=0$$ where $$a,b,d\\in\\mathbb{Z}$$. [3]\n (c) In the context of the question, explain the significance of the Voronoi cell containing site $$E$$. [1]',
