            question:
              "A manufacturer makes trash cans shaped as a cylinder with a hemispherical top, height $$70$$ cm, base radius $$20$$ cm (both cylinder and hemisphere). A designer produces a new trash can (same shape) with height $$H$$ cm and base radius $$r$$ cm, subject to the constraint $$H+2r=110$$ cm, maximizing volume.\n a. Write down the height of the cylinder (original trash can).\n b. Find the total volume of the (original) trash can.\n c. Find the height of the cylinder, $$h$$, of the new trash can, in terms of $$r$$.\n d. Show that the volume, $$V$$ cm$$^3$$, of the new trash can is given by $$V=110\\pi r^3-\\dfrac{7}{3}\\pi r^3$$ (equivalently $$V=110\\pi r^2 - \\dfrac{7}{3}\\pi r^3$$).\n e. Using your GDC, find the value of $$r$$ which maximizes $$V$$.\n f. The designer claims the new trash can's capacity is at least $$40\\%$$ greater than the original. State whether the designer's claim is correct, justifying your answer.",
