              'Haraya owns two triangular plots of land, ABC and ACD. $$AB=30$$ m, $$BC=50$$ m, $$AC=70$$ m, $$D\\hat{A}C=55°$$ and $$A\\hat{D}C=72°$$. Haraya attaches a $$20$$ m long rope to a vertical pole at point B.\n a. Find the length of AD.\n b. Find the size of $$A\\hat{B}C$$.\n c. Calculate the area of the triangular plot of land ABC.\n d. Determine whether the rope can extend into the triangular plot of land ACD. Justify your answer.',
