              'Let $$f(x)=\\dfrac{16}{x}$$. The line $$L$$ is tangent to the graph of $$f$$ at $$x=8$$. $$L$$ can be expressed as $$\\mathbf{r}=\\begin{pmatrix}8\\\\2\\end{pmatrix}+t\\mathbf{u}$$. The direction vector of $$y=x$$ is $$\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\1\\end{pmatrix}$$.\n a. Find the gradient of $$L$$.\n b. Find $$\\mathbf{u}$$.\n c. Find the acute angle between $$y=x$$ and $$L$$.\n d.i. Find $$(f\\circ f)(x)$$.\n d.ii. Hence, write down $$f^{-1}(x)$$.\n d.iii. Hence or otherwise, find the obtuse angle formed by the tangent to $$f$$ at $$x=8$$ and the tangent to $$f$$ at $$x=2$$.',
