            question:
              "Irina uses a set of coordinate axes to draw her design of a window. The base of the window is on the $$x$$-axis, the upper part of the window is in the form of a quadratic curve and the sides are vertical lines. The curve has end points $$(0,10)$$ and $$(8,10)$$ and its vertex is $$(4,12)$$. Distances are measured in centimetres. The quadratic curve can be expressed in the form $$y=ax^2+bx+c$$ for $$0\\le x\\le8$$.\n a.i. Write down the value of $$c$$. [1]\n a.ii. Hence form two equations in terms of $$a$$ and $$b$$. [2]\n a.iii. Hence find the equation of the quadratic curve. [2]\n b. Find the area of the shaded region in Irina's design. [3]",
