              'The voltage $$v$$ in a circuit is given by the equation $$v(t)=3\\sin(100\\pi t),\\ t\\ge0$$ where $$t$$ is measured in seconds.\n The current $$i$$ in this circuit is given by the equation $$i(t)=2\\sin(100\\pi(t+0.003))$$.\n The power $$p$$ in this circuit is given by $$p(t)=v(t)\\times i(t)$$.\n The average power $$p_{av}$$ in this circuit from $$t=0$$ to $$t=T$$ is given by $$p_{av}(T)=\\dfrac{1}{T}\\displaystyle\\int_0^T p(t)\\,dt,\\ T>0$$.\n a. Write down the maximum and minimum value of $$v$$. [2]\n b. Write down two transformations that will transform the graph of $$y=v(t)$$ onto the graph of $$y=i(t)$$. [2]\n c. Sketch the graph of $$y=p(t)$$ for $$0\\le t\\le0.02$$, showing clearly the coordinates of the first maximum and the first minimum. [3]\n d. Find the total time in the interval $$0\\le t\\le0.02$$ for which $$p(t)\\ge3$$. [3]\n e. Find $$p_{av}(0.007)$$. [2]\n f. With reference to your graph of $$y=p(t)$$ explain why $$p_{av}(T)>0$$ for all $$T>0$$. [2]\n g. Given that $$p(t)$$ can be written as $$p(t)=a\\sin(b(t-c))+d$$ where $$a,b,c,d>0$$, use your graph to find the values of $$a$$, $$b$$, $$c$$ and $$d$$. [6]',
            answer:
              'a. Max $$=3$$, min $$=-3$$\n b. Vertical stretch scale factor $$\\frac{2}{3}$$; horizontal translation of $$0.003$$ to the left\n c. Sinusoidal curve with first max at $$(0.0035, 4.76)$$ and first min at $$(0.0085,-1.24)$$\n d. $$0.00730$$ s\n e. $$p_{av}(0.007)=2.87$$\n f. Because the negative area under each cycle is smaller than the positive area, and the curve starts on the positive part\n g. $$a=3.00,\\ b=200\\pi\\ (\\approx628),\\ c=0.00100,\\ d=1.76$$',
            solution:
              'a. $$3, -3$$ (A1A1)\n b. Stretch parallel to the $$y$$-axis (with $$x$$-axis invariant), scale factor $$\\frac{2}{3}$$ (A1); translation of $$\\begin{pmatrix}-0.003\\\\0\\end{pmatrix}$$ (A1)\n c. Correct shape over correct domain with correct endpoints (A1); first max at $$(0.0035,4.76)$$ (A1); first min at $$(0.0085,-1.24)$$ (A1)\n d. $$p\\ge3$$ between $$t=0.0016762$$ and $$0.0053238$$, and between $$t=0.011676$$ and $$0.015324$$ (M1A1); total $$=0.00730$$ (A1)\n e. $$p_{av}=\\frac{1}{0.007}\\int_0^{0.007}6\\sin(100\\pi t)\\sin(100\\pi(t+0.003))\\,dt$$ (M1) $$=2.87$$ (A1)\n f. In each cycle the area under the $$t$$-axis is smaller than the area above it (R1); the curve begins with the positive part of the cycle (R1)\n g. $$a=\\frac{4.76-(-1.24)}{2}=3.00$$ (M1A1); $$d=\\frac{4.76+(-1.24)}{2}=1.76$$ (A1); $$b=\\frac{2\\pi}{0.01}=628\\,(=200\\pi)$$ (A1); $$c=0.0035-\\frac{0.01}{4}=0.00100$$ (M1A1)',
            questionType: 'Sinusoidal modelling, Transformations, Integration, GDC methods',
            diagram: null,
            subtopicSlug: 'trigonometric-functions-and-modelling',
