            marks: 17,
            marksBreakdown: null,
            calculator: true,
            question:
              'A sector of a circle, centre O and radius 4.5 m, is shown (chord AB, perpendicular distance from O to AB is 4 m). A square field with side 8 m has a goat tied to a post at the centre by a rope reaching 4.5 m from the post. Let V be the volume of grass eaten (m³) and t the time (hours) the goat has been in the field. The goat eats grass at rate $$\\dfrac{dV}{dt}=0.3\\,te^{-t}$$.\n (a)(i) Find the angle $$A\\hat{O}B$$. [3]\n (a)(ii) Find the area of the shaded segment. [5]\n (b) Find the area of the field that can be reached by the goat. [4]\n (c) Find the value of t at which the goat is eating grass at the greatest rate. [2]\n (d) The goat is tied in the field for 8 hours. Find the total volume of grass eaten during this time. [3]',
            answer:
              '(a)(i) $$A\\hat{O}B\\approx54.5°\\ (0.952\\ \\text{rad})$$\n (a)(ii) Segment area $$\\approx1.39\\ \\text{m}^{2}$$\n (b) Field area reached $$\\approx58.1\\ \\text{m}^{2}$$\n (c) $$t=1\\ \\text{hour}$$\n (d) $$\\approx0.299\\ \\text{m}^{3}$$',
            solution:
              '(a)(i) $$\\tfrac12A\\hat OB=\\arccos\\left(\\dfrac{4}{4.5}\\right)=27.27°\\Rightarrow A\\hat OB=54.5°$$ (M1A1A1).\n (a)(ii) Area of triangle $$=\\tfrac12(4.5)^2\\sin(54.53°)=8.25\\ \\text{m}^2$$; area of sector $$=\\dfrac{54.53}{360}\\pi(4.5)^2=9.64\\ \\text{m}^2$$; segment $$=9.64-8.25=1.39\\ \\text{m}^2$$ (M1A1M1A1A1).\n (b) Circle area $$\\pi(4.5)^2=63.62$$; subtract 4 segments: $$63.62-4(1.39)=58.1\\ \\text{m}^2$$ (A1A1M1A1).\n (c) Sketch $$dV/dt$$ or set $$d^2V/dt^2=0$$ (M1): $$t=1$$ hour (A1).\n (d) $$V=\\displaystyle\\int_0^8 0.3te^{-t}\\,dt\\approx0.299\\ \\text{m}^3$$ (M1A1A1).\n Verified with sympy: angle $$=54.53°$$, segment area $$=1.3904$$, field area $$=58.056$$, all match official mark scheme.',
