            marks: 21,
            marksBreakdown: null,
            calculator: true,
            question:
              'At an archery tournament, a ball is launched into the air while an archer attempts to hit it with an arrow. The path of the ball is modelled by $$\\begin{pmatrix}x\\\\y\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}5\\\\0\\end{pmatrix}+t\\begin{pmatrix}u_x\\\\u_y-5t\\end{pmatrix}$$ where x is horizontal displacement from the archer, y is vertical displacement from the ground (metres), t is time (s) since launch, $$u_x=8$$, $$u_y=10$$. An archer releases an arrow from $$(0,2)$$, travelling in a straight line at speed $$60\\,\\text{ms}^{-1}$$ and angle of elevation $$10°$$.\n (a)(i) Find the initial speed of the ball. [2]\n (a)(ii) Find the angle of elevation of the ball as it is launched. [2]\n (b) Find the maximum height reached by the ball. [3]\n (c) Assuming the ground is horizontal and the ball is not hit, find the x-coordinate where the ball lands. [3]\n (d) For the path of the ball, find an expression for y in terms of x. [3]\n (e) Determine the two positions where the path of the arrow intersects the path of the ball. [4]\n (f) Determine the time when the arrow should be released to hit the ball before the ball reaches its maximum height. [4]',
            answer:
              '(a)(i) $$12.8\\ \\text{ms}^{-1}$$\n (a)(ii) $$51.3°$$\n (b) $$5\\ \\text{m}$$ (at $$t=1$$)\n (c) $$x=21\\ \\text{m}$$\n (d) $$y=-\\dfrac{5}{64}(x-5)(x-21)$$\n (e) $$(8.66,3.53)$$ and $$(15.1,4.66)$$\n (f) $$t\\approx0.311\\ \\text{s}$$',
            solution:
              "(a)(i) $$\\sqrt{10^2+8^2}=12.8\\ \\text{ms}^{-1}$$ (M1A1).\n (a)(ii) $$\\arctan\\left(\\dfrac{10}{8}\\right)=51.3°$$ (M1A1).\n (b) $$y=t(10-5t)$$; maximum at $$t=1$$ (from symmetry or calculus), $$y=5\\ \\text{m}$$ (M1A1A1).\n (c) Solve $$t(10-5t)=0\\Rightarrow t=2$$ (excluding $$t=0$$); $$x=5+8(2)=21\\ \\text{m}$$ (M1A1A1).\n (d) $$t=\\dfrac{x-5}{8}$$; substitute into y-equation: $$y=\\dfrac{x-5}{8}\\left(10-5\\cdot\\dfrac{x-5}{8}\\right)$$, simplifying to $$y=-\\dfrac{5}{64}(x-5)(x-21)$$ (M1A1A1).\n (e) Arrow trajectory: $$y=x\\tan10°+2$$; intersect with the ball's path quadratic to find both intersection points: $$(8.66,3.53)$$ and $$(15.1,4.66)$$ (A1M1A1A1).\n (f) At the first intersection ($$x=8.657$$), the ball reaches that point at $$t_{\\text{target}}=\\dfrac{8.657-5}{8}=0.457$$ s; distance from arrow's release point to intersection $$\\approx8.791$$ m; time for arrow to travel there at 60 ms⁻¹ $$=0.1465$$ s; release time $$=0.457-0.1465\\approx0.311$$ s (A1M1A1A1).\n Verified with sympy: initial speed $$=12.806$$, angle $$=51.34°$$, max height at $$t=1$$ gives $$y=5$$ — all match official mark scheme.",
            questionType: 'Vector kinematics, projectile motion, simultaneous equations',
            diagram: null,
            subtopicSlug: 'kinematics',
