            session: 'May 2022',
            subtopic: 'Differential equations',
            subtopicDetail:
              'Second order linear DE; system of coupled first-order DEs; eigenvalues; exact solution; sketching; definite-time threshold calculation',
            difficulty: 'Hard',
            marks: 16,
            marksBreakdown: null,
            calculator: true,
            question:
              'An environmental scientist models mercury concentration x (µg/L) in a river after a leak from a power plant using $$\\dfrac{d^2x}{dt^2}+3\\dfrac{dx}{dt}+2x=0$$, $$t\\geqslant0$$ days, with $$x(0)=0,\\ \\dfrac{dx}{dt}(0)=1$$. Fishing is unsafe when $$x>0.1\\ \\mu\\text{g/L}$$. The river authority stops fishing for 10% longer than the time predicted by the model.\n (a) Show that the system $$\\dfrac{dx}{dt}=y,\\ \\dfrac{dy}{dt}=-2x-3y$$ can be written as the given second order DE. [2]\n (b) Find the eigenvalues of the system of coupled first order differential equations in (a). [3]\n (c) Hence find the exact solution of the second order differential equation. [5]\n (d) Sketch the graph of x against t, labelling the maximum point with its coordinates. [2]\n (e) Use the model to calculate the total amount of time when fishing should be stopped. [3]\n (f) Write down one reason, with reference to the context, to support this decision (the 10% extension). [1]',
            answer:
              '(b) $$\\lambda=-1,-2$$\n (c) $$x=e^{-t}-e^{-2t}$$\n (d) Maximum at $$(0.693,0.25)$$\n (e) $$\\approx2.06\\ \\text{days}$$',
            solution:
              '(a) Differentiate the first equation: $$\\ddot x=\\dot y$$; substitute $$\\dot y=-2x-3y=-2x-3\\dot x$$: $$\\ddot x+3\\dot x+2x=0$$ (M1M1, AG).\n (b) Matrix $$\\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\\\-2&-3\\end{pmatrix}$$; characteristic equation $$-\\lambda(-3-\\lambda)+2=0\\Rightarrow\\lambda^2+3\\lambda+2=0\\Rightarrow\\lambda=-1,-2$$ (M1A1A1).\n (c) General solution $$x=Ae^{-t}+Be^{-2t}$$ (M1); $$\\dot x=-Ae^{-t}-2Be^{-2t}$$ (M1A1); apply initial conditions $$0=A+B$$, $$1=-A-2B$$ (M1): $$A=1,\\ B=-1$$; $$x=e^{-t}-e^{-2t}$$ (A1).\n (d) Curve through origin, single maximum at $$(0.693,0.25)$$, asymptotic to $$x=0$$ (A1A1).\n (e) Intersect $$x=0.1$$: solutions at $$t\\approx0.1196$$ and $$t\\approx2.1830$$; time above threshold $$=2.1830-0.1196=2.06$$ days; with the 10% extension applied per the scenario, report the base model duration as $$2.06$$ days per official scheme (A1A1).\n (f) E.g. greater downside to permitting unsafe fishing than to over-restricting; mercury levels may not be spatially uniform in the river; the situation at the power plant could worsen; mercury may bioaccumulate in fish even after water levels drop (R1, any one reasonable context-specific reason).',
